From ab0f88faff66986db1b47af517ac430ec824df67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:42:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(thread): external threads on a boss at the operation
 level

The Thread operation gains `external`: its list then holds bosses
(major radius, top, shoulder), read from the model by Detect holes
(`drilling::recognize_bosses`: the hole recogniser's law with the facing
vote inverted, stepped walls never folded) and passed to the kernel's
external ride pinned by #1005.

A tool beside a boss is judged without the part's silhouette:
- crest law: the tangency verdict against each boss's MINOR circle
  (ISO 965-1 design root, 0.6134 x pitch) - the drawn wall is not the
  wall the crests answer to (#1071's lesson read for a boss);
- root law: the solid law with the cutter narrowed by the external
  depth - roots, tip, shank and holder against the whole part;
- neighbour law (new): the crest ring at full radius against every
  facet that is not the threaded boss's own wall, no thread allowance.

The air law (#992's external analogue): every position the feeds take
the tool through is read in the stock the program ahead leaves; stock
standing under the tool's disc outside the boss refuses the thread by
name. Unknown is refused.

The door refuses a boss no thicker than the thread is deep and a thread
longer than the mill reaches beside a boss. The program simulation
sweeps an external thread at its external root radius. The Thread page
gets the external checkbox, Detect bosses and a per-row Remove; the MCP
tools carry the flag through the existing params and detect_holes.

Goldens: thread_mill_external_m8_multi_form.cl/.nc,
thread_mill_external_m10_single_form.cl.

Fixes #985

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
