From 29e097c9e6ba99aa9b2d408080b363565bebf399 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:25:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(thread): refuse an external thread on a boss that is
 not round

The crest law reads each boss's minor circle and the neighbour law passes
the boss's own wall, both taking that wall for a circle. A hex stud or a
square post stands its flats inside the drawn circle, where the teeth
would cut them with no law reading them. thread_boss::not_round applies
the internal side's walls_round test (verify::hole_is_round, the solid
law's sagitta test) to the boss wall, and generate refuses a boss that
fails it by name. Pinned by
thread_boss::a_hex_stud_is_no_round_boss_and_is_refused_by_name; the
decision is in docs/decisions/985-external-threads.md.

Refs #985

